flowchart TB
  accTitle: Turn shared information into collaborative intelligence
  accDescr: A member contributes contextualised observations. Peers correlate, enrich and validate them. Information that meets the quality threshold for a proposed use can support detection or response. Information below that threshold remains available for analysis when policy allows. Sightings, corrections, uncertainty and outcomes feed back into updated shared information and the next assessment.

  contribute["Contribute observations<br/>with context and provenance"]:::accent
  assess["Correlate, enrich<br/>and validate"]
  threshold{"Meets the quality threshold<br/>for the proposed use?"}
  act["Use in detection<br/>or response"]:::success
  analyse["Keep for analysis<br/>when policy allows"]:::muted
  feedback["Return sightings, corrections,<br/>uncertainty and outcomes"]
  update["Update shared information<br/>within its handling rules"]:::accent

  contribute -->|Peers review| assess
  assess -->|Assess confidence and relevance| threshold
  threshold -->|Yes| act
  threshold -->|Not yet| analyse
  act -->|Report results| feedback
  analyse -->|Report findings| feedback
  feedback -->|Improve the contribution| update
  update -->|Reassess as evidence changes| assess
